<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Sweden in good shape for EMU - Asbrink.</title>
<headline>Sweden in good shape for EMU - Asbrink.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Finance Minister Erik Arbrink reiterated on Saturday that entry into the EU's exchange rate mechanism was not a current issue in Sweden, but that he was &quot;more and more convinced&quot; that the country would meet EMU entry criteria with a good margin.</p>
<p>&quot;I think we will be in a strong position in 1997,&quot; Asbrink told Reuters Financial Television.</p>
</text>
